goscape-singleplayer — third-party notices and attribution
==========================================================

goscape-singleplayer contains no ported game code of its own. It is a launcher:
it links the goscape server and the goscape-client game client into a single
process and wires them together over loopback TCP. Everything it runs is
attributed in those two projects' own NOTICE files, which travel with the
modules this binary depends on.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
goscape — the server
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

https://github.com/zsrv/goscape, MIT-licensed. A from-scratch Go rewrite of the
Lost City TypeScript RuneScape server (https://github.com/LostCityRS/Engine-TS,
MIT). Its NOTICE additionally covers the pkg/dskit port of Grafana's
Apache-2.0 dskit and its build scaffolding:

    https://github.com/zsrv/goscape/blob/main/NOTICE

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
goscape-client — the game client
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

https://github.com/zsrv/goscape-client, MIT-licensed. A Go port of the
RuneScape 2 client, translated from the Lost City project's Client-Java and
Client-TS (https://github.com/LostCityRS). See its NOTICE for the full
attribution, including the Client-TS license text:

    https://github.com/zsrv/goscape-client/blob/main/NOTICE

